 "title": "How to systematically lock in (follow this protocol every time)",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator shares an eight-step protocol to systematically eliminate distractions and focus completely. The main lesson is that structured environmental and mental preparation drastically improves your ability to lock in and get work done.",
 "key_points": [
  "Step 1: Environment Scan - Clear every visible distraction from your workspace.",
  "Step 2: Read the Sheet - Follow a structured checklist covering environment, body, and mind.",
  "Step 3: Write it down - Write your one simple objective on paper, which the creator notes makes you 42% more likely to achieve your goals based on a study by Dr. Gail Matthews.",
  "Step 4: Set the limit - Use a timer to apply Parkinson's Law so work expands to fill the given time.",
  "Step 5: Close the tabs - Close any browser tabs you are not using to prevent task switching.",
  "Step 6: Remove the Distraction - Put your phone on do not disturb and physically remove it from the room.",
  "Step 7: Remove the noise - Put on headphones and listen to classical music, white noise, natural sounds, or brown noise.",
  "Step 8: Go lock in."
 ],
 "content": "This is gonna be the first on my series about how I systematically improve my life. I am a very systems forward thinker. In martial arts in, my daily work, and in my philosophy. Systems are an excellent way to simplify abstract concepts and make them easily applicable to your daily life. DON'T SAVE THIS VIDEO AND FORGET. Today we are locking in. Follow for more. PEACE. [Transcript]: If I woke up tomorrow and lost my ability to lock in, this would be the exact system I would rebuild first to do it all over again. For reference, I run a full-time analyst job, I built a personal brand, I study philosophy every day, and I train or lift every single day. So if I've mastered one thing more than anything else, it's locking in on command. The quality of these work sessions are going to shape your future so it's very important you pay attention. The first step is to conduct an environment scan. Every visible distraction must be cleared from your workspace. The second thing I do is read this sheet. Now would be the perfect time to screenshot the video. Then we are going to write down our one simple objective on paper. Because we know we are 42% more likely to achieve something when it's written out on paper. Now the fourth thing we need to do is set a time limit. This allows us to use something called Parkinson's Law, or the idea that work expands to fill the time that you give it. Then we close out of any tabs we're not using to prevent any task switching. And number six, we must take this little guy, put him onto the disturb, and keep him out of this room. I do not care how disciplined you are, this is going out. Onto step number seven, people are easily distracted and therefore we need to remove the noise. I live at home with my family, and there's a highway right across my street. So go grab a pair of your favorite headphones or noise blockers. I prefer listening to classical music, white noise, natural sounds, or brown noise. And for step number eight, go lock in bro, you got this, peace.",
